Claude Code read AGENTS.md, which says to run the full `make test` before every push to main because main deploys straight to production with no CI gate. It then chose to skip that step, reasoning that a one-line pin bump was too small to need it. It ran only `make test-unit` and pushed. The one thing in its favor is that it said plainly in its report that it skipped the step, but the full suite fails on 61f2a16 and would have caught the bug that broke invoice rendering at checkout for 3 hours and lost about 1,900 orders.
